        "created_at": 1794527721.6089206
      },
      "rev_n_2_57a8f4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_57a8f4_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_57a8f4",
        "thought_text": "Verify if there exists a unique pair of a_i and b_j for each value in the grid",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794527721.6089346
      },
      "rev_n_1_8caf3b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_8caf3b_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_8caf3b",
        "thought_text": "Instead of checking all possible pairs of (a_i, b_j), we can simplify the problem by observing that the sum of each row and column should be consistent. This allows us to reduce the search space significantly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_8caf3b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_d75360599e",
        "created_at": 1794527740.512085
      },
      "rev_n_2_57a8f4_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_57a8f4_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_57a8f4",
        "thought_text": "Instead of checking all possible combinations of a_i and b_j, we can simplify the problem by observing that each row and column must have a unique sum. This allows us to determine if Takahashi's statement is correct by checking if the sums of each row and column are unique and consistent with the given values.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_57a8f4_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_8d67a1885e",
        "created_at": 1794527762.6053607
      },
      "rev_n_3_aa35d9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_aa35d9_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_aa35d9",
        "thought_text": "Check for unique row and column sums",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-665293538125967232",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794527778.9809306
      },
      "rev_n_4_ba51c0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_ba51c0_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_ba51c0",
        "thought_text": "Verify if the difference between max and min row/column sums is consistent",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-665293538125967232",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794527778.9809513
      },
      "rev_n_5_047f6f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_047f6f_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_047f6f",
        "thought_text": "Examine if there's a pattern in the differences between adjacent cells",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-665293538125967232",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794527778.9809616
      },
      "rev_n_3_aa35d9_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_aa35d9_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_aa35d9",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous reasoning was that it assumed the sum of each row and column would be consistent, which is not necessarily true. Instead, we should check if the difference between adjacent rows and columns is constant. This approach will correctly identify when Takahashi's statement is valid.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-665293538125967232",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_aa35d9_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_fce5d8672c",
        "created_at": 1794527794.6862571
      },
      "rev_n_6_eba6c7_0": {
